    23	
    24	At a fixed angular frequency, let the two transverse components of a stationary source have cross-spectral density
    25	
    26	\[
    27	W_{ij}(r_1,r_2)=\mathbb E[E_i(r_1)E_j(r_2)^*].
    28	\]
    29	
    30	This convention is the complex conjugate/transposed convention of some optics references; observables are unchanged. A physically realizable source has a positive-semidefinite matrix kernel. A polarization-independent deterministic scalar kernel produces
    31	
    32	\[
    33	J_{ij}(x)=\iint K(x,r_1)W_{ij}(r_1,r_2)K(x,r_2)^*\,dr_1dr_2.
    34	\]
    35	
    36	Define intensity \(I=\operatorname{tr}J\), and, **only where \(I>0\)**,
    37	
    38	\[
    39	P(J)=\sqrt{1-4\det J/(\operatorname{tr}J)^2}
    40	     =|\boldsymbol s|/s_0,\qquad
    41	J=(s_0I_2+\boldsymbol s\cdot\boldsymbol\sigma)/2.
    42	\]
    43	
