   511	   - **Depolarizing branch:** trace-support dimension two and
   512	     \(\Psi(X)=P_\star U XU^\dagger+(1-P_\star)\operatorname{tr}(X)I_2/2\), \(0\leq P_\star\leq1\).
   513	   - **Transpose-depolarizing branch:** trace-support dimension two and
   514	     \(\Psi(X)=P_\star U X^{\mathsf T}U^\dagger+(1-P_\star)\operatorname{tr}(X)I_2/2\), \(0\leq P_\star\leq1/3\).
   515	
   516	Here \(U\) is an arbitrary polarization unitary and the transpose is in the fixed whitened radial basis. The two-mode proof and complete-positivity endpoint conditions are the already proved C2, now legitimately applicable by the response lemma. Rank-one trace support can only give replacement; all dark directions are handled as above.
   517	
   518	For **all** physical covariances in the class, first choose any permitted nonzero sum block \(K\), then choose an arbitrary Hermitian \(L\) with
   519	\[
   520	0\preceq L\preceq K,\qquad \Gamma_+=L,\quad \Gamma_-=K-L.
   521	\tag{SPLIT}
   522	\]
   523	Conversely every solution has exactly this description, because its two sector covariances are PSD and sum to \(K\). Neither sector must have degree \(P_\star\) by itself. The class includes C6: its sum block is
   524	\(\operatorname{diag}(1,1/2)\otimes\operatorname{diag}(3/4,1/4)\), a replacement sum, while its full spatial trace support has rank four. ∎
   525	
   526	### Precisely supported isotropic-ABCD corollary
   527	
   528	The same classification is equivalent to invariance under **every centered, lossless, polarization-independent isotropic real ABCD system**, with \(AD-BC=1\), in the scalar paraxial model. For \(B\neq0\), its Collins kernel is proportional to
   529	\[
   530	\exp\!\left[\frac{ik}{2B}
   531	\left(A r'^2+D r^2-2rr'\cos(\theta-\theta')\right)\right].
   532	\]
   533	Angular integration has the same \(J_{\pm m}\) identity as Fresnel propagation, so it produces common radial amplitudes \(q_0,q_1\) for the two azimuthal sectors. Thus (SUM) still holds and the classified sum block preserves the degree for those amplitudes. For \(B=0\), common scalar magnification and quadratic phase give the same conclusion directly. Necessity follows because forward Fresnel systems are members of this ABCD family. No density assertion for one fixed ABCD system is needed.
   534	
   535	This does **not** cover astigmatism, polarization-dependent Jones kernels, cross-azimuthal-sector covariance, general other radial modes, random ensemble averaging, or full Maxwell propagation. C6's astigmatic negative control is deliberately retained.

